<task id="013" project="spaarkeai-compose-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-05 create-on-save pipeline — extend PromoteIfEphemeralAsync (container/record/index; profile deferred to core)</title>
    <phase>1 Entry</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <estimated-hours>18</estimated-hours>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <dependencies>none</dependencies>
    <blocks>014,015,017</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api,api,dataverse,spe</tags>
    <rigor-hint reason="Core persistence pipeline; modifies .cs backbone; BFF + Dataverse + SPE; FULL per TASK-INDEX">FULL</rigor-hint>
    <model-tier reason="Architectural pipeline change enforcing the R5-E persistence invariant across container/record/indexing; high blast radius; opus per TASK-INDEX">opus</model-tier>
    <parallel-group>W2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe reason="BFF-only (ComposeService + SPE/Dataverse + the promote/save DTO); does not touch the ComposeWorkspace/ComposeEmptyState files 010/011/012 edit">true</parallel-safe>
    <rescope date="2026-07-09" by="owner" decision="Option 1">
      Original scope assumed a SERVER-SIDE business-unit→SPE-container primitive that does not exist (spec Unresolved Q#2; escalated 2026-07-09, three coupled forks A/B/C — see notes/defer-issues.md "Open architectural escalations"). Owner chose Option 1:
      • Fork A (BU→container) → CLIENT resolves the container id (existing wizard cascade `resolveBusinessUnitContainerId`) and passes it INTO the promote/save request. This IS the existing matter/project-creation convention (§6.5 path C, pivot-to-comply). Reject a new BFF resolver (contradicts multi-container INV-7 + project CLAUDE.md).
      • Fork B (transient contract) → when the request carries no existing `DocumentSpeId`, this task CREATES the SPE drive-item in the supplied container under OBO before record/index. IN SCOPE (server half). The client half (supplying `containerId` + transient bytes on Save) couples to 010/012 → tracked as a small frontend follow-on, NOT this task.
      • Fork C (profile analysis) → the `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IDocumentProfileAi` facade is CORE's (redesign-r2) surface — handed off (notes/HANDOFF-to-core-profile-analysis-facade.md). This task treats profile as a NON-BLOCKING DEFERRED step: it emits a `deferred` job state for profile and back-fills when core ships the facade. Profile is OUT of this task's implementation.
      INTERIM R5-E bar (documented exception, tied to core delivering C): a record with NO SPE file OR NO index is NEVER success; a record that is stored + created + indexed with profile=`deferred` IS acceptable interim success. The full R5-E bar (incl. profile) is restored when core ships `IDocumentProfileAi`.
    </rescope>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    `ComposeService.PromoteIfEphemeralAsync` already runs on every Save and half-implements creation:
    idempotently it creates the `sprk_document` row + a new SPE version and rebinds the ChatSession. FR-05
    (Option-1 re-scope) upgrades it to the create-on-save BACKBONE: accept a CLIENT-SUPPLIED container id on
    the promote/save request (Fork A), CREATE the SPE drive-item in that container when the request has no
    existing `DocumentSpeId` (Fork B — transient Browse/Upload/AI-drafted drafts), create the `sprk_document`,
    and run INDEXING via the existing `IPostUploadIndexingEnqueuer` (sync-OBO). PROFILE ANALYSIS is a
    NON-BLOCKING DEFERRED step (Fork C is core-owned — see &lt;rescope&gt;): emit a `deferred` job state for it, do
    not implement it here. Interim R5-E: a record with no SPE file or no index is NEVER success; stored + created
    + indexed with profile=`deferred` IS interim success. Idempotency preserved. Optional parent-association is a
    SEPARATE task (014). Per-step OutcomeCard rendering is core-A0-gated (`JobAwareCompletionState`) and NOT in
    scope — this task PRODUCES the per-step job states the card will later render (core's projector already names
    the four steps `container → record → profile-analysis → indexing`).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET developer fluent in Minimal API, SharePoint Embedded (SpeFileStore facade), Dataverse
    document creation, and the Spaarke indexing pipeline + Job Contract. You extend an existing, idempotent
    service method to the create-on-save backbone without breaking its idempotency, and you honor the
    escalation-resolved boundary (container comes from the client; profile is deferred to core).
  </role>

  <goal>
    First Save of a transient draft runs a create-on-save backbone: (1) validate the CLIENT-SUPPLIED container
    id (fail the `container` step honestly if absent), (2) when no `DocumentSpeId` is supplied, create the SPE
    drive-item in that container under OBO, (3) create `sprk_document`, (4) run indexing via
    `IPostUploadIndexingEnqueuer`, (5) emit a `deferred` state for profile-analysis (core-owned). Each step emits
    a distinct job-aware state (queued/running/deferred/partial/completed/failed) via the existing Job Contract,
    projected through `JobAwareCompletionStateProjector`. The method stays idempotent; a fileless or unindexed
    record is never returned as success; a profile-deferred record IS interim success.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Create-on-save half-exists in `PromoteIfEphemeralAsync` (idempotent; creates row + SPE version + rebinds).
      The escalation (2026-07-09) established: the BU→container resolution is client-side and passed into the BFF
      (Fork A); transient drafts have no SPE drive-item so Save must create one (Fork B); the only profile seam is
      `IAppOnlyAnalysisService` which trips the ADR-013 NetArchTest facade rule and runs under MI (likely 403 on the
      OBO-written file) — so profile is deferred to a core-owned `IDocumentProfileAi` facade (Fork C). Indexing
      (`IPostUploadIndexingEnqueuer.EnqueueIfApplicableAsync`) is sync-OBO, always-registered, ADR-013-safe — use it.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file purpose="extend-backbone" edit="true">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs</file>
      <file purpose="promote/save-DTO" edit="true">the promote/save request DTO (add client-supplied ContainerId; carry transient bytes/no-DocumentSpeId case) — locate in ComposeService.cs or its request models</file>
      <file purpose="save-endpoint" edit="maybe">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file purpose="spe-facade" edit="false">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/**/SpeFileStore*.cs — drive-item create + OBO write via facade (ADR-007)</file>
      <file purpose="indexing-seam" edit="false">the IPostUploadIndexingEnqueuer registration + EnqueueIfApplicableAsync signature</file>
      <file purpose="step-projection" edit="false">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/JobAwareCompletionState*.cs — Projector.Project(JobContract, IReadOnlyList&lt;StoredStepSignal&gt;, observedAt); already names container→record→profile-analysis→indexing</file>
      <file purpose="background-jobs" edit="false">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/ServiceBusJobProcessor.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <notes>
      `PromoteIfEphemeralAsync` ~line 203, invoked from the Save path ~line 186. Container id is now an INPUT
      (client-supplied) — do NOT resolve it server-side. Drive-item creation for the no-DocumentSpeId case goes
      through the SpeFileStore facade under OBO. Profile step: enqueue nothing, emit `deferred` — a placeholder the
      future core facade + a re-profile pass will satisfy. Indexing runs sync-OBO (the Compose user holds the file
      ACL; MI does not — same constraint that deferred profile).
    </notes>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">`Services/Compose` never injects `IOpenAiClient`/executor/routing types; do NOT inject `IAppOnlyAnalysisService` (would trip NFR-05 NetArchTest). Profile is deferred to core's facade, not reached here.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">No `Microsoft.Graph` types above the SpeFileStore/Infrastructure facade — container drive-item creation + SPE writes go through the facade.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-005">SPE storage follows the flat-storage container model; a container id is REQUIRED for persistence (now client-supplied — validate presence).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-001">Any long-running step is a Minimal-API/`BackgroundService`/Job-Contract flow — no Azure Functions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Keep `Services/Compose` DI additions minimal; internal helpers need not be DI-registered.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (interim R5-E, exception 2026-07-09)">A `sprk_document` with no SPE file OR no index is NEVER success. A stored + created + indexed record with profile=`deferred` IS acceptable interim success (full R5-E incl. profile restored when core ships `IDocumentProfileAi`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Preserve idempotency: re-Save of an already-promoted document does not double-create the row, container, or drive-item.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Container id is CLIENT-SUPPLIED (Fork A) — do NOT add a server-side BU→container resolver.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Profile analysis is OUT (Fork C, core-owned) — emit `deferred`, do not implement.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Parent association is OUT (task 014); do NOT block creation on a parent — a standalone Document is valid.</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-hygiene">BFF-touching — state Placement Justification, measure publish-size delta vs 49.63 MB baseline, run CVE scan, add/update tests per §10.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>compose/create-on-save, spe-ingestion, dataverse-document, background-jobs, job-aware-completion</topic>
