  <justification component="Extended create-on-save backbone (extends PromoteIfEphemeralAsync)">
    <existing>`PromoteIfEphemeralAsync` already creates the row + SPE version + rebinds; `IPostUploadIndexingEnqueuer` + the Job Contract + `JobAwareCompletionStateProjector` exist as platform primitives.</existing>
    <extension>Extend the existing method to accept a client-supplied container id, create the drive-item for transient drafts, chain indexing, and project per-step states; no new service class beyond internal helpers. Profile deferred to core.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it, a transient Browse/Upload/AI-drafted draft cannot be saved at all — the entire create→edit→save→find loop is dark, and success criterion #4 (first Save yields a real, searchable Spaarke Document) fails.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Load spec.md FR-05 + `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` + notes/defer-issues.md "Open architectural escalations". State Placement Justification. Read `PromoteIfEphemeralAsync` + the Save path + the promote/save DTO; confirm the `IPostUploadIndexingEnqueuer` signature + the `JobAwareCompletionStateProjector` seam.</step>
    <step order="1">Add a CLIENT-SUPPLIED `ContainerId` (+ transient-bytes / no-`DocumentSpeId` case) to the promote/save request DTO. Validate container presence; fail the `container` step honestly if absent (do NOT resolve server-side).</step>
    <step order="2">When no `DocumentSpeId` is supplied, create the SPE drive-item in the supplied container via the `SpeFileStore` facade under OBO. Keep the existing idempotent `sprk_document` creation + rebind.</step>
    <step order="3">Chain indexing via `IPostUploadIndexingEnqueuer.EnqueueIfApplicableAsync` (sync-OBO). Emit a `deferred` job state for profile-analysis (core-owned; not implemented here).</step>
    <step order="4">Emit per-step job states (container/record/profile-analysis[deferred]/indexing) and project via `JobAwareCompletionStateProjector` so a fileless/unindexed record is never success while profile-deferred is interim success. Return the projected state shape the future OutcomeCard renders.</step>
    <step order="5">Add/update unit tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/ per NFR-08 (incl. negatives: missing container → container step fails; no-DocumentSpeId → drive-item created; fileless/unindexed → not success; profile-deferred → interim success; re-Save idempotent). Build BFF; measure publish-size; CVE scan; NetArchTest facade green (proves profile NOT injected).</step>
    <step order="6">Run code-review + adr-check (Step 9.5). Update TASK-INDEX + current-task.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">the promote/save request DTO (client-supplied ContainerId)</output>
    <output type="code" optional="true">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/ComposeServiceCreateOnSaveTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">First Save of a transient draft validates a CLIENT-SUPPLIED container id and persists the file there; missing container fails the `container` step honestly (no server-side resolver).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">When the request carries no `DocumentSpeId`, the SPE drive-item is created in the supplied container under OBO before record/index.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Creation produces `sprk_document` + indexing, each with a distinct job-aware state; profile-analysis emits a `deferred` state (not implemented here).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">(negative, interim R5-E) A record lacking an SPE file OR an index is never returned as success (partial/failed). A stored+created+indexed record with profile=`deferred` IS interim success.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The method remains idempotent: re-Save of an already-promoted document does not double-create the row, container, or drive-item.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Creation does NOT require a parent association (a standalone Document is valid).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `Microsoft.Graph` type leaks above the SpeFileStore facade (ADR-007); `Services/Compose` injects no AI internals incl. no `IAppOnlyAnalysisService` (ADR-013); NetArchTest facade rule green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish-size delta reported vs 49.63 MB baseline; no new HIGH CVE; unit tests (incl. all negatives) pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the client-supplied-container contract cannot be added additively (e.g., the promote/save DTO is shared in a way that forces a breaking change), OR indexing cannot run OBO for the Compose-written file, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6/§6.5 rather than guessing.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>

  <notes date="2026-07-09" status="completed">
    Implemented the Option-1 create-on-save backbone in ComposeService.SaveAsync (not a new method):
    • Fork A — added client-supplied `ContainerId` (+ made `DocumentSpeId`/`DriveId` nullable) to
      SaveComposeDocumentRequest; missing container fails the `container` step honestly (returns a
      Failed-aggregate result, no server-side BU→container resolver).
    • Fork B — when `DocumentSpeId` is absent, creates the SPE drive-item in the supplied container
      under OBO via ISpeFileOperations.UploadSmallAsUserAsync (surfaced the already-implemented
      SpeFileStore method on the interface — minimal ADR-007-preserving facade extension). Existing
      item → replace-content path unchanged. Idempotent: drive-item created only when SpeId absent;
      row creation reuses the existing alt-key idempotency.
    • Indexing — sync-OBO via IPostUploadIndexingEnqueuer.EnqueueIfApplicableAsync (new ctor dep;
      unconditional registration, no asymmetric-registration risk).
    • Fork C — profile-analysis emitted as a DEFERRED step (Queued + "deferred" detail; no Deferred
      enum member exists). NO IAppOnlyAnalysisService injected — ADR013_ComposeFacadeTests green.
    • Result shape — SaveComposeDocumentResult.CompletionState carries the 4-step
      JobAwareCompletionStateProjector projection (container→record→profile-analysis→indexing);
      aggregate Partial on happy path (profile deferred). Interim R5-E bar exposed as
      ComposeService.IsInterimCreateOnSaveSuccess (container+record+indexing all Completed);
      fileless/unindexed never success.
    DEVIATION: edited ISpeFileOperations.cs (outside literal file list) — additive, only prod impl
    is SpeFileStore which already implements it; documented in adr-check.
    ComposeEndpoints.cs NOT edited (client/HTTP half is the frontend follow-on; all 10 routes preserved).
    Verify: BFF build 0 errors; Compose unit tests 232 pass (224 prior + 8 new); Compose endpoint
    contract 15/15; facade arch test 1/1; publish 45.19 MB compressed (−4.44 vs 49.63 baseline);
    CVE = pre-existing Microsoft.Kiota.Abstractions HIGH only (no new packages).
  </notes>
</task>
